{"yuDisWira":[{"id":"yuDizWira","headword":"युधिष्ठिर","headword_slp1":"yuDizWira","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"9. Yudhiṣṭhira ("},{"t":"cite","s":"No. 28","q":"No"},{"t":"txt","s":", "},{"t":"cite","s":"L. 24","q":"L"},{"t":"txt","s":"; "},{"t":"cite","s":"No. 29","q":"No"},{"t":"txt","s":", "},{"t":"cite","s":"L. 16","q":"L"},{"t":"txt","s":"; "},{"t":"cite","s":"No. 35","q":"No"},{"t":"txt","s":", "},{"t":"cite","s":"L. 12","q":"L"},{"t":"txt","s":";\n"},{"t":"cite","s":"No. 36","q":"No"},{"t":"txt","s":", "},{"t":"cite","s":"L. 17","q":"L"},{"t":"txt","s":"; "},{"t":"cite","s":"No. 43","q":"No"},{"t":"txt","s":", "},{"t":"cite","s":"L. 33","q":"L"},{"t":"txt","s":"; "},{"t":"cite","s":"No. 44","q":"No"},{"t":"txt","s":", "},{"t":"cite","s":"L. 24","q":"L"},{"t":"txt","s":"; "},{"t":"cite","s":"No. 52","q":"No"},{"t":"txt","s":",\n"},{"t":"cite","s":"L. 14","q":"L"},{"t":"txt","s":"):\n[]\nHe is mentioned in the imprecatory verses and is described\nas the best of kings. Literally meaning ‘firm or steady in\nbattle’, it was the name of the eldest of the five sons of Pāṇḍu.\nHe was father of Prativindhya and Sudhanu and before his\ndeath installed his grandson Parīkṣita on the throne (at Has-\ntinapur) and Vajra at Mathurā.^80"}]}]}]}